   "evidence": "`LinearMap.mkContinuous_apply` is the explicit unfolding lemma and is used as such in Mathlib: `Mathlib/Analysis/Normed/Module/Bases.lean:513` (`simp only [..., LinearMap.mkContinuous_apply, ...]`).",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/Analysis/Normed/Algebra/MatrixExponential.lean",
   "fix": "Obtain `h := HasFDerivAt.comp_hasDerivAt t L.hasFDerivAt (hasDerivAt_exp_smul_const_comp hf A)` without ascribing the type, then finish with `simpa only [L, LinearMap.mkContinuous_apply, LinearMap.coe_mk, AddHom.coe_mk, Function.comp_def, mulVec_mulVec, \u2190 smul_mulVec] using h`.",
   "issue": "`hL` is closed by `rfl` through the `LinearMap.mkContinuous`/`ContinuousLinearMap` coercion, and the `have h` type ascription (line 71) likewise relies on `\u21d1L \u2218 g` being defeq to `fun s => g s *\u1d65 v`. Both break if Mathlib changes how `mkContinuous` is bundled.",
   "line": 78
  },
  {
   "evidence": "After `\u2190 integratedCoupling_add S.alphaS_continuous \u03c4\u2080 \u03c4\u2081 \u03c4\u2082` the only difference between the two sides is the cast of a real sum and the summand order; no structural congruence is needed.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/QFT/Factorization/Evolution/MomentSpace.lean",
   "fix": "Replace `congr 2; push_cast; ring` with `rw [Complex.ofReal_add, add_comm]` (or `simp [Complex.ofReal_add, add_comm]`).",
